        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Fountain Hill, Bethlehem, Pennsylvania, Lehigh Valley, Freemansburg, Bethlehem Township, Hanover Township, Lehigh County, Northampton County\n- Organizations: Bethlehem Area School District\n- Topics: population, municipal coverage\n\nFacts:\n- Fountain Hill is a suburb of Bethlehem, Pennsylvania, in the Lehigh Valley region of Pennsylvania.\n- As of the 2010 census, Bethlehem, Pennsylvania, had a population of 74,982 and was the seventh largest city in Pennsylvania after Philadelphia, Pittsburgh, Allentown, Erie, Reading, and Scranton.\n- The Bethlehem Area School District covers the City of Bethlehem, the boroughs of Fountain Hill and Freemansburg, and Bethlehem Township and Hanover Township in Lehigh County and Northampton County.",
